Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 04:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: the cursor clip stays inside the virtual screen.

The PS5 display modes are emulated: a 640x480 mode is drawn letterboxed on the 1920x1080 display, so the raw
coordinates the server keeps the clip in are the physical screen's. With no clip the server's rect is that whole
screen, and mapped back into the 640x480 mode it is (-107,0)-(747,480), where Windows reports the screen,
(0,0)-(640,480). Wine's d3d9 test checks it after a fullscreen mode change (device.c:14950); it showed on the Pro
once the desktop could be made the foreground (patch 2151), which leaves the cursor unclipped there, and passes on the
PC, whose mode changes are real. GetClipCursor now keeps the mapped rect inside the virtual screen, as Windows keeps
every clip.
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/input.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/input.c
@@ -2791,7 +2791,14 @@
     while ((status = get_shared_desktop( &lock, &desktop_shm )) == STATUS_PENDING)
         *rect = wine_server_get_rect( desktop_shm->cursor.clip );
 
-    if (!status && type == MDT_EFFECTIVE_DPI) *rect = map_rect_raw_to_virt( *rect, dpi );
+    if (!status && type == MDT_EFFECTIVE_DPI)
+    {
+        RECT virtual_rect = get_virtual_screen_rect( dpi, MDT_DEFAULT );
+
+        /* in an emulated display mode the unclipped raw rect is the whole physical screen, wider than the mode */
+        *rect = map_rect_raw_to_virt( *rect, dpi );
+        intersect_rect( rect, rect, &virtual_rect );
+    }
     return !status;
 }
 
